# *******************************************************************
# refalabclg_dbg
# Compile a RefalAB program, link it with the standard initiator and run it.
# Debug version: no optimization, debug information, the debug library and the debug trace.
# arg: $1 - name of the RefalAB program (without the extension .ref)
# result: the program $1_dbg is built and run (the log is in $1_dbg.log)
# *******************************************************************

# Compile to the object file through LLVM IR; the compiler listing goes to the log file.
bin/refalabc $1 -l,"-o $1_dbg.o -O0 -g -Wno-override-module" > $1_dbg.log
# Link the object file with the standard initiator and the library; the linker messages are appended to the log file.
clang -o $1_dbg $1_dbg.o lib/obj/refalab_initiator_dbg.o -Llib -lrefalab_dbg >> $1_dbg.log
# Run the program.
$1_dbg
